    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/7/1/71780.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 27,
    "turn_text": "Well, I think that you have the shifting demographics. You know, case in point, you have Toyota North America moved their headquarters from California here to North Texas. And you have 50 of the Fortune 500 businesses that are here in Texas. And Texas has the number 11 largest economy in the world. And so you're right, all of these great conservative policies that enable small business growth and corporations and businesses to come here. But people aren't talking to those employees and getting them to understand why they moved their corporations here to Texas. And then we have to be concerned about, you know, the flooding of illegal immigrants into the state of Texas. And that's why the left does not want to have a citizenship question on the census. They believe that representation should just be based upon numbers and not numbers of citizens. That can have a very detrimental effect here in Texas.",
