  {
    "episode_id": 71780,
    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/7/1/71780.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 35,
    "turn_text": "i think that there's a bit of reticence and recalcitrance i mean you know let's just go back and say what was the original problem The original problem was that you had people that were, you know, above that poverty line, but they were in that gap of the quote unquote work and poor. And there's some very simple policies that we could implement. We can expand the use of health savings accounts. I mean, they need to be able to better articulate the problem, better articulate the solution. Of course, it's very hard to run against people that are just saying we're going to give it to everyone for free to include illegal immigrants. But I think that as Ronald Reagan would say, you got to paint those bold colors and not the pretty pastels. And I think sometimes Republicans still get hung up on pretty pastels.",
