        "confidence": 0.96
      },
      {
        "text": "People value ease and immediate gratification when making political choices.",
        "confidence": 0.93
      },
      {
        "text": "Younger voters and economically disadvantaged individuals prioritize material benefits over effort.",
        "confidence": 0.91
      },
      {
        "text": "The speaker believes that earning through work is morally superior to receiving handouts.",
        "confidence": 0.9
      },
      {
        "text": "Political appeals based on entitlement undermine long-term societal responsibility.",
        "confidence": 0.88
      }
    ],
    "turn_type_label": "Substantive",
    "conversation_move_label": "Agree / Align"
  },
  {
    "episode_id": 71780,
    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/7/1/71780.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 37,
    "turn_text": "Well, you know, interestingly enough, a lot of the rhetoric that you hear coming out of these progressive socialist candidates of the Democrat Party a lot of things that were paraded by Hugo Chavez down in Venezuela who took one of the most prosperous countries in our hemisphere and now look at it. And I think it's important we have to express, Scott, that free is not freedom because every time people promise you this and promise you that, it comes with a price. And normally the price that comes along with that is your individual freedom, your individual liberty, your individual rights.",
